      <Comment>|FRAME: Vernolates Vernolate| (vernolic acid) is a fatty acid with an 18-carbon chain that contains a &lt;i&gt;cis&lt;/i&gt; double bond at position 9 and an epoxy group at positions 12-13. Like other fatty acids, |FRAME: Vernolates| is rarely found in its free form. It is usually found |FRAME: Glycerolipid-vernolate &quot;incorporated into a lipid&quot;|. When studied in planrts, the compound is usually referred to as &quot;vernolic acid&quot;. When studied in mammals, it is referred to as &quot;isoleukotoxin&quot;.</Comment>
